# == Alonzo ==

# REPO.1: the Cargo workspace's build output, including the wasm the
# allowlist check reads. Cargo.lock is NOT ignored: the workspace will hold
# a binary (the native runner the frame floors need), so the lockfile is
# committed from the first build.
target/

# ENGINE.1: the page tools/build_web.ps1 will write from
# web/index.template.html and the wasm engine, Frazaro's split: the template
# is source, the filled page is output.
web/index.html

# Scratch area for throwaway experiments, so they never clutter history.
scratch/

# Editor and operating-system residue.
~$*
*.tmp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
